Found a real behavioral difference in postBulkBugsCreation:

**Old code** in the newBugs create path:
```js
var priority = bugDef.priority || 'Medium';
var result = getTracker().createTicket(projectKey, 'Bug', summary, description);
```
Note: `priority` is computed but... let me check the createTicket signature. Old passes `(projectKey, 'Bug', summary, description)` — priority was computed but NOT passed? Let me check: `getTracker().createTicket(projectKey, 'Bug', summary, description)` — yes, only 4 args in both old and new. In the new code `tryCreateBulkBug(summary, description, linkedTCs)` also passes 4 args. So priority was unused in both. Fine — equivalent.

**Description resolution order difference:** 

Old:
```js
var description = null;
if (bugDef.descriptionFile) { description = readFile(...); if (!description) warn }
if (!description && linkedTCs.length > 0) { failedReason... }
if (!description) { description = summary; }
```

New `resolveBugDescription`:
```js
var description = readBugDescriptionFile(bugDef.descriptionFile); // null if !descriptionFile
if (description) return description;
return failedReasonOrSummary(ctx, summary, linkedTCs);
```
`failedReasonOrSummary`: if linkedTCs.length === 0 return summary; failedReason = getFailedReasonForTc(linkedTCs[0]...) — wait, but the old code only called getFailedReasonForTc when `linkedTCs.length > 0`. New also guards. Same. But note: in old code, if descriptionFile was missing/not found, it warns 'descriptionFile not found' — new readBugDescriptionFile also warns. But new warns only `if (!descriptionFile) return null` — no warn when descriptionFile is falsy (not provided). Old: if bugDef.descriptionFile falsy, no warn. Same.

**BUT there's an important difference in the order of operations!** In the OLD code, the description was resolved (including the getFailedReasonForTc tracker call) BEFORE the `findAnyLinkedNonDoneBug` live re-check. In the NEW code (`processNewBugDef`):

```js
var existingBugKey = findAnyLinkedNonDoneBug(linkedTCs);
if (existingBugKey) { linkExistingBugForTcGroup(...); return; }
createAndDistributeBug(ctx, bugDef, summary, linkedTCs, plan);
```

and description resolution happens inside `createAndDistributeBug` — AFTER the live re-check. So when an existing bug is found, the old code still called `getFailedReasonForTc` (a tracker getIssue call) before the re-check; the new code skips it. That changes "same tracker/SCM calls in the same order" — the failed-reason getIssue call is dropped in the live-recheck path. Side effect difference: fewer tracker calls when an existing bug is found. This is a behavior change (albeit arguably an improvement) — ticket says "Same tracker/SCM/git calls in the same order". Worth flaging as IMPORTANT (behavior deviation), since it also affects: the console.warn 'descriptionFile not found' no longer fires in the recheck path, and 'ℹ️ Using Failed Reason' log. Also the readFile of descriptionFile no longer happens in recheck path. Impact: minor. I'll flag as IMPORTANT or SUGESTION. Given the ticket's strict "same calls in same order" rule, I'd say IMPORTANT.

