⚠️ **IMPORTANT: Live re-check moved before description resolution — tracker/file call sequence changed**

The old `newBugs` loop resolved the bug description **before** the live re-check:

```javascript
// old order
var description = readFile(bugDef.descriptionFile);   // file_read tool call
if (!description && linkedTCs.length > 0) {
    var failedReason = getFailedReasonForTc(...);     // tracker getIssue call
}
console.log('  Creating bug:', summary, ...);
var existingBugKey = findAnyLinkedNonDoneBug(linkedTCs);
```

In the refactored `processNewBugDef` the re-check runs first and `createAndDistributeBug` (which holds `resolveBugDescription`) only runs when a new bug is actually created. Consequences in the live-recheck path (`existingBugKey` found):

1. `file_read(descriptionFile)` is no longer called.
2. The Failed-Reason fallback (`getIssue` via `getFailedReasonForTc`) is skipped — **one fewer tracker API call**, violating the ticket rule "Same tracker/SCM/git calls in the same order".
3. The `'  Creating bug:'` log line is no longer emitted before the re-check (old code logged it even when the re-check found an existing bug).

None of the 33 new tests pin this path's call sequence (the recheck test mocks `file_read` but never asserts it was invoked), so the drift is invisible to the suite. The fix is small: resolve the description (and log) before `findAnyLinkedNonDoneBug`, or hoist description resolution into `processNewBugDef` before the re-check, matching the original order.

